haracterization of an interleukin-7-dependent thymic cell line derived from a p53(&#x02212;/&#x02212;) mouse. <source>J. Immunol. Methods.</source> <volume>274</volume>:<fpage>177</fpage>&#x02013;184.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12609543</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal">Kondrack, R.M., J. Harbertson, J.T. Tan, M.E. McBreen, C.D. Surh, and L.M. Bradley. <year>2003</year>. Interleukin 7 regulates the survival and generation of memory CD4 cells. <source>J. Exp. Med.</source> <volume>198</volume>:<fpage>1797</fpage>&#x02013;1806.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14662907</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><citation citation-type="journal">Lavoie, J.N., G. L'Allemain, A. Brunet, R. Muller, and J. Pouyssegur. <year>1996</year>. Cyclin D1 expression is regulated positively by the p42/p44MAPK and negatively by the p38/HOGMAPK pathway. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>271</volume>:<fpage>20608</fpage>&#x02013;20616.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8702807</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib26"><citation citation-type="journal">Li, J., G. Huston, and S.L. Swain. <year>2003</year>. IL-7 promotes the transition of CD4 effectors to persistent memory cells. <source>J. Exp. Med.</source> <volume>198</volume>:<fpage>1807</fpage>&#x02013;1815.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14676295</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib27"><citation citation-type="journal">Li, W.Q., Q. Jiang, A.R. Khaled, J.R. Keller, and S.K. Durum. <year>2004</year>. Interleukin-7 inactivates the pro-apoptotic protein bad promoting T cell survival. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>279</volume>:<fpage>29160</fpage>&#x02013;29166.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15123689</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib28"><citation citation-type="journal">Mailand, N., J. Falck, C. Lukas, R.G. Syljuasen, M. Welcker, J. Bartek, and J. Lukas. <year>2000</year>. Rapid destruction of human Cdc25A in response to DNA damage. <source>Science.</source> <volume>288</volume>:<fpage>1425</fpage>&#x020