 Rathmell, and C.B. Thompson. <year>2001</year>. Akt and Bcl-xL promote growth factor-independent survival through distinct effects on mitochondrial physiology. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>276</volume>:<fpage>12041</fpage>&#x02013;12048.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11278698</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib36"><citation citation-type="journal">Rajnavolgyi, E., N. Benbernou, B. Rethi, D. Reynolds, H.A. Young, M. Magocsi, K. Muegge, and S.K. Durum. <year>2002</year>. IL-7 withdrawal induces a stress pathway activating p38 and Jun N-terminal kinases. <source>Cell. Signal.</source> <volume>14</volume>:<fpage>761</fpage>&#x02013;769.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12034357</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib37"><citation citation-type="journal">Schluns, K.S., and L. Lefrancois. <year>2003</year>. Cytokine control of memory T-cell development and survival. <source>Nat. Rev. Immunol.</source> <volume>3</volume>:<fpage>269</fpage>&#x02013;279.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12669018</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib38"><citation citation-type="journal">Schluns, K.S., W.C. Kieper, S.C. Jameson, and L. Lefrancois. <year>2000</year>. Interleukin-7 mediates the homeostasis of naive and memory CD8 T cells in vivo. <source>Nat. Immunol.</source> <volume>1</volume>:<fpage>426</fpage>&#x02013;432.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11062503</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib39"><citation citation-type="journal">Seddon, B., P. Tomlinson, and R. Zamoyska. <year>2003</year>. Interleukin 7 and T cell receptor signals regulate homeostasis of CD4 memory cells. <source>Nat. Immunol.</source> <volume>4</volume>:<fpage>680</fpage>&#x02013;686.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12808452</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib40"><citation citation-type="journal">Sexl, V., J.A. Diehl, C.J. Sherr, R. Ashmun, D. Beach, and M.F. Roussel. <year>1999</year>. A rate limiting function of cdc25A for S phase entry inversely correlates with tyrosine dephosphorylation of Cdk2. <source>Oncogene.</source> <volume>18</volume>:<fpage>573</fpage>&#x02013;582.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9989807</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib41"><citation citation-type="journal">Shimuta, K., N. Nakajo, K. Uto, Y. Hayano, K. Okazaki, and N. Sagata. <year>2002</year>. Chk1 is activated transiently and targets Cdc25A for degradation at the <italic>Xenopus</italic> midblastula transition. <source>EMBO J.</source> <volume>21</volume>:<fpage>3694</fpage>&#x02013;3703.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12110582</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib42"><citation citation-type="journal">Sorensen, C.S., R.G. Syljuasen, J. Falck, T. Schroeder, L. Ronnstrand, K.K. Khanna, B.B. Zhou, J. Bartek, and J. Lukas. <year>2003</year>. Chk1 regulates the S phase checkpoint by coupling the physiological turnover and ionizing radiation-induced accelerated proteolysis of Cdc25A. <source>Cancer Cell.</source> <volume>3</volume>:<fpage>247</fpage>&#x02013;258.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12676583</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib43"><citation citation-type="journal">Tan, J.T., E. Dudl, E. LeRoy, R. Murray, J. Sprent, K.I. Weinberg, and C.D. Surh. <year>2001</year>. IL-7 is critical for homeostatic proliferation and survival of naive T cells. <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source> <volume>98</volume>:<fpage>8732</fpage>&#x02013;8737.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11447288</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib44"><citation citation-type="journal">Trede, N.S., E. Castigli, R.S. Geha, and T. Chatila. <year>1993</year>. Microbial superantigens induce NF-kappa B in the human monocytic cell line THP-1. <source>J. Immunol.</source> <volume>150</volume>:<fpage>5604</fpage>&#x02013;5613.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8515079</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib45"><citation citation-type="journal">Vander, H.M., N.S. Chandel, P.T. Schumacker, and C.B. Thompson. <year>1999</year>. Bcl-xL prevents cell death following growth factor withdrawal by facilitating mitochondrial ATP/ADP exchange. <source>Mol. Cell.</source> <volume>3</volume>:<fpage>159</fpage>&#x02013;167.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10078199</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib46"><citation citation-type="journal">Vidal, A., and A. Koff. <year>2000</year>. Cell-cycle inhibitors: three families united by a common cause. <source>Gene.</source> <volume>247</volume>:<fpage>1</fpage>&#x02013;15.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10773440</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>